  {
   "key": "scene_02",
   "text": "City arrive with 1 win in their last 5 matches, and without the injured Antoine Semenyo. Fulham have 2 wins and 2 draws. There is also a cloud over the club. In September, a commission found City guilty of 114 of the 115 Premier League financial charges. City are appealing, and no sanction is set yet. So a question hangs over this run: is the case weighing on the players? Maresca, the day before: \"I don't think the players are focused on the noise.\" Former City midfielder Didi Hamann disagrees. He tells Sports Mole the uncertainty is a factor. Fulham's Álvaro Arbeloa calls his team's 20 straight defeats against City not relevant.",
