  {
   "key": "scene_07",
   "text": "Here is what the scoreline hides. FotMob's numbers give City 1.87 xG, and Fulham 0.74. Whatever Maresca feared at the back, Fulham got little. So why only one goal? Not the goalkeeper. Bernd Leno's goals prevented figure is below zero, so he did not save Fulham. The cause is simpler. Only 3 of City's 15 shots were on target. The other 12 were blocked or missed the goal. Two big chances, none scored. Haaland's was saved, and Rúben Dias's header at minute 42 missed the target. The numbers point to shots that never tested the keeper.",
