  {
   "key": "scene_08",
   "text": "FotMob rates Elliot Anderson 8.1, the highest of any player. The lowest among City's starters is Haaland, on 6.5: 4 shots, 1 on target, no goal. So is Haaland working less? In the 5 games he has played since 24 October, he ran between 9377 and 9866 metres in each. Against Fulham he ran 9654, and made 13 sprints, his most in that run. His 24 touches were his most too. The effort is there. The finishing is not. Against Fulham, Haaland's problem was the last touch, not the running.",
