  {
   "key": "scene_09",
   "text": "Maresca asked for fewer avoidable goals. So who let this one in? It began with a Fulham throw-in deep in their own half. Muniz won the ball in the air, then ran the length of the pitch on the counter. Bobb beat his man and found him in the box. Squawka's analysis says City's midfield faltered. So not the defence alone. In our reading, City lost the ball in the air, and no one stopped the break. One chance, worth only 0.14 xG, was enough. Two questions for the comments. Was Muniz's goal avoidable? And is the case weighing on City's players? Tell us below, and subscribe.",
